  "body": "Adds preserved Bengali Riyadh al-Salihin source files and a source-context reader. Readers can inspect original pages, notes, explanations and provenance without treating the 2,029 source occurrences as a unique hadith count. Source IDs, recorded ambiguities and qualified ledger references remain intact; held occurrences are not added to verified narration counts.\n\nThe repository retains all 252 manifest-bound source and evidence assets, including the original DOC and PDF files. The website stages the compact reader and both PDFs for page links; the DOC files and full evidence remain accessible through immutable repository links. The reader's compressed embedded data decodes byte-for-byte to the previously reviewed source data. A Git attribute protects checksum-bound source bytes, and public validation accepts documents only after the source-context manifest and Bengali binding gate verify them.\n\nThe earlier full rebuild exceeded the existing 950 MB site budget. With compact source staging, the passing GitHub build measured 905,998,985 bytes against the unchanged 950,000,000-byte budget on tested base bd4a75695d3c695e98bf8efa5ce07764ac5e2633.\n\nValidation: GitHub passed all 994 software tests, the full bank rebuild and the Chromium reader check. The compact and upstream-reconciled version also passed 31 affected Linux tests and the Node source-panel test, including occurrence-specific grouped-source rendering. Independent review found no blocking issue in the compressed payload, 252 asset hashes, site staging, PDF requirements or reconciliation with the newer grouped reader. A local site fixture and Chromium check covered search, source context, PDF links and the 9,067-passage explorer; all 15 immutable evidence and DOC links passed HEAD checks. These targeted checks do not represent an independent reread of the whole book.\n\nThe branch includes the tested upstream checkpoint without replacing its work. Main has since advanced; a conflict-free local trial merge preserved the reviewed files and workflow timeouts. Coordinate with the active importer before merging, then verify the integrated build, deployment and live source links.",
